.TH SDL_IsMainThread 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_IsMainThread \- Return whether this is the main thread.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_init.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_IsMainThread(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
On Apple platforms, the main thread is the thread that runs your program\(aqs main() entry point\[char46] On other platforms, the main thread is the one that calls
.BR SDL_Init ([SDL_INIT_VIDEO](SDL_INIT_VIDEO)),
which should usually be the one that runs your program\(aqs main() entry point\[char46] If you are using the main callbacks,
.BR SDL_AppInit (),
.BR SDL_AppIterate (),
and
.BR SDL_AppQuit ()
are all called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true if this thread is the main thread, or false otherwise\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

